    {
      "id": "claim_624c3777350547a4afa46eac1b288e7d",
      "statement": "sse_send calls `let _ = tx.send(..)`, deliberately ignoring a send failure whether the channel has no receivers or is full. Progress is therefore best-effort telemetry and not a work queue: on a headless server with no browser attached every event is silently discarded, and no client-side behaviour may depend on delivery — the authoritative state is re-read from SQLite.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/server.rs#L70-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d7d77c3cb5cd7f7b55d5ef2673c6412d5d14f43a5f57d04be5bacdd9096eb901:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_42aa21f89c9e4613a39f34736d0ccf4a",
      "statement": "GET /events is served by sse_handler, which calls sse_tx.subscribe() per connection (so each client sees every event) and wraps an async_stream loop in Sse::new(..).keep_alive(KeepAlive::default()) so an idle stream keeps emitting keep-alive comments. Inside the loop a RecvError::Lagged(n) only logs a warning and continues — a slow client loses messages but keeps its connection — while RecvError::Closed and cancel.cancelled() both break the loop and end the response.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/server.rs#L1066-L1099",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb3d4b89f950d88d58a480c4289f051b7addb68199798e39bf29c6be2689f271:"
        },
