          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc7ef3941b7b56e157bc13e0056347405e286ebb981b3c03273d36a058bea9b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d50d5eb3a9d42a7a09168dabc2ff56e",
      "statement": "spawn_cli_action is the template for GraphQL-triggered long work: it emits {prefix}_started, then acquires its database connection *inside* the spawned task and runs the CLI subcommand, and emits {prefix}_complete with success:true or {prefix}_error with success:false plus a human-readable message. Acquiring after `started` is what guarantees a pool-exhaustion failure surfaces as {prefix}_error instead of silence — the invariant being that every code path emits exactly one terminal event.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/mutation.rs#L21-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab7ee87c606dc34614d447b3dca7e51fd961560fac84d13805d720a8c2adec8f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f418729ebe714698b82e1aa9d421508d",
      "statement": "The event prefixes actually emitted by the web server are: sort_roms, check_roms, generate_playlists, purge_roms, convert_roms and purge_irds via spawn_cli_action; download_dats and purge inlined in the download_dats and purge_system mutations (note the system-purge prefix is `purge`, not `purge_system`); and import_dat, import_rom, import_patch and import_irds from the four multipart upload handlers, each of which returns 202 Accepted and reports only over SSE.",
