    {
      "id": "claim_606cd9a978ff4f359d974cff36a5c64a",
      "statement": "The MCP bridge and the GraphQL helper differ in when an action becomes visible on /events: run_action takes the process-wide write lock and acquires a pooled connection *before* sending {prefix}_started, so an MCP action queued behind another writer is invisible to the browser until it actually begins, whereas spawn_cli_action announces {prefix}_started before waiting for a connection.",
