    {
      "id": "claim_01a609abb519466fa9cd3cbc598aa400",
      "statement": "Progress-bar movement is not bridged into SSE: every GraphQL action and upload handler runs on ProgressBar::hidden() and SSE carries only lifecycle events with their message string. MCP is the only bridge — run_action creates a visible none-style bar with start_action so there is something to read, then (only when the caller passed a progressToken) spawns a poller that sleeps 400 ms, samples (position, length, message) from the subcommand-owned bar, and sends notifications/progress solely when that tuple changed, giving up when notify_progress fails and being aborted as soon as the work settles.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/mcp/actions.rs#L86-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92d189dcb7257a65cbff55eacb98a76c8edef1fdca32d0351f2b8e2ba4a21b46:"
