    {
      "id": "claim_5041b004e1874eb88417d5f16b76e6c9",
      "statement": "import_dat is the one prefix that can emit several terminal events for a single request: process_dat_upload returns a Vec<Result<ImportDatResult>> — one entry per DAT inside an uploaded ZIP — and the task sends import_dat_complete per Imported/UpToDate entry (skipped: true for the latter) or import_dat_error per failure, while ImportDatResult::Skipped (an --update against a system that does not exist) is filtered out by results.retain before the handler sees it and emits nothing at all.",
