    {
      "id": "claim_24fc3201bab046228958e07d00905f0e",
      "statement": "shutdown_signal waits for Ctrl+C or (on unix) SIGTERM, runs optimize_database (incremental_vacuum, optimize, wal_checkpoint(truncate)) and only then calls cancel.cancel(), so /events streams stay open for the duration of the checkpoint before all terminating together. The shared token breaks every SSE receive loop and unblocks in-flight MCP actions, which race work against the per-request ctx.ct ('cancelled by the client') and self.cancel ('server shutting down'); spawned CLI actions from GraphQL mutations and uploads are not watched for cancellation and run to completion.",
