    {
      "id": "claim_3ecd7a664c8546fab2d6dbf5b95b6c09",
      "statement": "No test exercises /events or MCP progress notifications: the server tests boot the real main() and assert only HTTP status codes (202 accepted, 400 rejected) or re-query GraphQL after a sleep, and tests/mcp_stdio.rs builds tools/call params without a progressToken so the progress poller never runs under test. Its hand-rolled client reads stdout until a line carries its own id (so unsolicited notifications are tolerated) and close() asserts a clean exit on stdin EOF. Consequently the SSE event names and payload shapes are an unverified contract — renaming a prefix compiles cleanly, silently breaks the matching SPA listener, and fails no test.",
