    {
      "id": "claim_2d2289fffbe24a15a1ed8038138f95a2",
      "statement": "The byte-level progress that ultimately reaches MCP clients comes from a workspace-wide contract: each format crate entry point takes `progress: &mut dyn FnMut(u64)` called with the input bytes consumed since the last call, adding up to the input size, and run_blocking in src/progress.rs adapts that callback to `bar.inc(n)` on a bytes-styled bar of `length` moved onto the blocking pool. Callers supply the matching total — the input file's metadata().len() for xso-rs/nsz/xdelta/xps, chd_rs::cd_input_size for a CD image, gdi_rs::input_size for GDI, and the CHD's info().logical_size when extracting — so those byte counts are precisely the position/total pair the poller forwards.",
